Match each cloud-computing benefit with the appropriate requirement.  

Each benefit can be used once, more than once, or not at all.

<DragDrop
  items={["Disaster recovery","Geo-distribution","High availability","Scalability"]}
  slots={[{"answer":"High availability","id":"slot1","label":"Provide a continuous user experience in the event of a resource failure."},{"answer":"Geo-distribution","id":"slot2","label":"Deploy apps and data to regional data centers that are located close to users."},{"answer":"Scalability","id":"slot3","label":"Compute capacity can be increased dynamically by adding RAM or CPU to a virtual machine."}]}
  reuse={true}
  explanation={"High availability maintains service when a resource fails. Geo-distribution deploys workloads in regions near users to reduce latency. Scalability increases available compute capacity, including by adding CPU or RAM to a virtual machine."}
